_refine_special_details          
;
The compound crystallized in P2/n with half of a 
molecule in the asymmetric unit and one iodine atom 
located on a two-fold rotation axis. The CpiPr5 ligand 
showed positional disorder over two sites, and the 
occupancies of these two components were refined while 
constraining the sum to unity, yielding a ratio of 
0.749(7):0.251(7). The refinement of the disordered CpiPr5 
ligand was stabilized through application of enhanced rigid 
bond restraints to the displacement parameters of the five 
carbons in the cyclopentadienyl ring and to the displacement 
parameters of the isopropyl groups. Two carbons in the 
cyclopentadienyl ring and three methyl carbons could not be 
stabilized unless identical anisotropic displacement parameters 
were utilized, which were determined by analogous carbon atoms 
in the disordered CpiPr5 ligand. In addition, one reflection 
(0 0 2) was omitted from the refinement due to large differences 
in I(obs) and I(calc), as recommended by the PLAT934 alert. This 
reflection was likely affected by the beamstop. 
;
